The code has multiple instances where security-relevant behavior depends on untrusted, unchecked, or unauthenticated data. Most notably:
(1) share accounting uses unchecked arithmetic on `u128` in several places, which can overflow/underflow and corrupt collateral/borrow balances;
(2) the LP-vs-regular position type is selected purely by a string prefix, and LP token IDs are converted into `AccountId` via `new_unchecked`, meaning the contract does not sufficiently verify the authenticity/validity of identifiers before using them in sensitive pricing/collateral logic;
(3) several `unwrap()`/`expect()` paths depend on attacker-controlled `token_id` presence in maps and can cause panics (DoS) if these methods are reachable with arbitrary inputs.
